    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38103" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπανα-μένω</span></b> , poet. <b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπαμμένω</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>wait longer,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				8.141
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Ar.
				<u>Ec.</u>
				790
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>wait for</i> one, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τινά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Nu.</u>
					803
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐ. τινὰ ἐλθεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Lys.</u>
					74
				</span></i>
			: impers., <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὅ τι μ᾽ ἐπαμμένει
			παθεῖν</span> what <i>there is in store</i> for me to suffer,
				<i><span class="en">
				A.
				<u>Pr.</u>
				605
			</span></i> (lyr.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὗ σφιν κακῶν ὕψιστ᾽ ἐπαμμένει
					παθεῖν</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Id.
					<u>Pers.</u>
					807
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τίς ἄρα με πότ μος . .
				ἐπαμμένει;</span> (<i><span class="en">
				Herm.
			</span></i> for <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐπιμένει</span>) <i><span class="en">
				S.
				<u>OC</u>
				1718
			</span></i>.</div>
